Qev is a Qwen-based decision-model research implementation. It was developed as
BranchKev before extraction into this repository. The selective extraction and
source-file hashes are recorded in provenance.json.

This project adapts conventions and implementation ideas from Kev:
  https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev
  Reviewed revision: 557598fced1dada75dfbf36ed144dce309ac6ceb
  Copyright 2026 Jared Palmer
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Adapted components include the reserved Qwen delimiter convention, text rendering
conventions, LoRA target selection, and the inference cache-fork approach.
Qev's candidate-tree encoding, set decision head, data adapters, and training
runner are maintained separately. Files extracted for this release were renamed
and modified for standalone Qev packaging, portable checkpoints and user-data
training. The original Kev attribution is retained in LICENSE and this notice.

Qwen models and Hugging Face Transformers are external dependencies. The optional
JevBench preparer downloads an independently versioned MIT-licensed upstream
snapshot from https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench and retains its license.
No Qwen base weights or original benchmark questions are redistributed in Git.

Model weights and datasets retain their respective terms. This source-code
license does not relicense third-party datasets or imply that the full research
training corpus is included.
